cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FaunaPulse in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "FaunaPulse: an Android field application for on-device detection, tracking and documentation of flower-visiting insects"
abstract: >-
  FaunaPulse is an offline Android field application that detects, tracks and
  documents flower-visiting insects (and other moving organisms) in real time
  using on-device object detection, and logs each visit to estimate visitation
  rates. It supports configurable detection models, a user-defined region of
  interest, motion-triggered capture and time-lapse capture.
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-pulse"
url: "https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-pulse"
# TODO: update `version` and `date-released` to match each tagged release.
version: "0.6.4"
date-released: "2026-07-20"
keywords:
  - pollinators
  - visitation rate
  - pollination ecology
  - on-device AI
  - object detection
  - insect monitoring
  - camera trap
  - Android
